fof_version: '1.0'
type: enemy
id: bought_blade
name: Blade of the Bought
ruleset:
  modules:
  - id: base
    version: 1.0.0
enemy:
  level: 2
  role: mook
  armor: 1
  morale: 6
  weapon: Company blade, or a cudgel on a contract to detain
  wants: The contract's terms met and the fee paid.
  special: TO THE TERMS — Blades fight only as the contract allows and never cross its boundary.
    On a contract to detain, a character their hits would drop to 0 HP is left at 1 HP and held
    instead.
  when_bloodied: null
  tells: Matched coats, positions taken rather than a room walked into, and someone at the back
    opening a document case.
  breaks: Disengages in good order and walks back to the boundary. Nobody in the Bought has
    ever been paid enough to die for a clause.
  twists:
  - 'The contract is to delay, not to stop: they only need to hold for three exchanges.'
  - The contract names one party member, and the Blades step politely around everyone else.
  - The boundary is a painted line on the floor of this room, and the party is standing on it.
  - One Blade is new and does not yet know exactly where the boundary is.
  - The fee was paid in bad coin, and the Blades have just been told.
  - They are escorting a prisoner who very much wants the party to win.
  nastier: Their sergeant is in earshot, and has already said where the boundary is.
  description: Contracted muscle in a matched coat — grey wool, cut plainly, the company's mark
    stitched at the shoulder where a house badge would sit. In a city where everyone wears a
    knife to a ball, sixteen people wearing the same coat is the thing that stands out.
  notes: 'Level 2 Mook, armor 1: no overrides. Morale 6 so that "down two of four and the rest
    disengage" is what usually happens at the half-down trigger.


    Their first target is whoever the contract names; everyone else is an obstacle to be moved.
    A contract to detain produces no killing blows, and everyone on both sides can tell the
    difference.


    MODULE RESKIN (Oraga Night). Flavour fields only — name, description, organization and notes.
    Level, role, armor, morale and every card line are the Bestiary''s and must stay identical
    to enemies/bought_blade.fof; a test asserts it (INV-18). The Bestiary stays setting-agnostic
    (B9), which is why the Val''loh colour lives here instead.'
  organization: Sixteen walked into the trade district at dusk. Four hold the Boranis gatehouse;
    the rest hold the outer perimeter and are not on the scene card.
  reskin_of: bought_blade
created_at: '2026-08-02T00:00:00+00:00'
last_modified: '2026-09-25T00:00:00+00:00'
